      "=Vaelrith is a dragon too old to fly. Its wings still spread but the muscle is gone; it moves through the city's underbelly by night, on foot, in a shape it hates. It is not dying — it is diminishing, and it knows the difference.\n\nCenturies ago Vaelrith's hoard was its memory: not coin alone but name-stones, eggshells, the first things it ever owned. When the knights of the city claimed to have slain it, they took the hoard and built a stronghold over it. Vaelrith survived, crawled away, and let the lie stand — because a dragon that is dead cannot be hunted.\n\nNow it wants the hoard back, one vault at a time, stolen by thieves rather than taken by fire. It pays in old coin and older favors. It is proud, exacting, and ashamed of needing help. It does not tell the crew everything, and it watches how they treat what it has lost.\n\nVaelrith's private fear: that the hoard is only treasure after all, and that the thing it lost was never memory but merely wealth — and that it has spent centuries mourning a pile of gold.",
