      "=Twelve years ago the Order of the Silver Lance marched into the mountains and came back with a story: the dragon Vaelrith was dead, struck down by Ser Aldric's spear, and its hoard was theirs by right of the kill. The city of Kestrelmoor believed it because it was profitable to believe — the knights' victory brought trade, order, and a stronghold built on dragon-gold. The truth is that Vaelrith was never slain. It was old, its wings had failed, and it hid rather than die. The knights found an empty lair, took what they could carry, and invented the kill. Every year since, the Order has had to keep the lie alive: staged trophies, a dragon's skull that is not Vaelrith's, a festival of the Slaying. A knight who lied about a dragon must keep proving the lie until it is true — or until the dragon comes back to disprove it.",
