      "=What the knights took from Vaelrith was never only gold. Beneath the coin and the crowns, in the deepest vault of the stronghold, they keep the things a dragon cannot replace: unhatched eggs gone cold, name-stones carved with the true names of Vaelrith's line, and memory-stones that hold the wyrm's own recollections of the centuries before the false slaying. The knights cannot spend any of it — the stones will not answer them and the eggs will not warm — so they keep it as proof of a kill they never made. Vaelrith does not fully remember what is down there; age has taken as much as the thieves did. Returning the memory-hoard may restore what the dragon was, or reveal that what it was is gone for good. The crew's choice of what to carry out of that vault decides which.",
