      "=Quill doesn't look up from the lock she's picking — a practice lock, worn smooth from years of the same motion. \"So. A dragon wants its own gold stolen back from the men who say they killed it.\" She sets the pick down and finally meets your eyes. \"That's either the best job I've ever heard or the last one. Which is it?\"",
